+/// absent-or-unsupported-entry rule forbids, and the record would then fail again on its next
+/// reader with nothing to say it was already known-damaged before the gateway served a byte.
+/// Named like every other audit seam in the tree (`wyrd.read.audit`, `read.rs:488`;
+/// `wyrd.custodian.gc.audit`, `crates/custodian/src/gc.rs:524`) so one filter selects the
+/// operator's repair queue.
