+/// everything already on disk. Otherwise a new-key PUT reuses a committed inode id, a bogus
+/// "concurrent writer won" conflict, because [`create`] is `require_absent` on the inode key
+/// (issue #364 durability finding 1). This walk supplies the mark `Gateway::recover` seeds
+/// that counter from (`crates/server/src/lib.rs:145-148`).
